## 60-day evaluation

A 60-day **free evaluation** is granted to any person or organization
to install, run, and integrate the official release artifacts of zlsx —
the compiled binaries and Python wheels published on the project's
releases page — for the purpose of deciding whether to obtain a
commercial license. The evaluation does not include any license to the
source code: compiling the source, modifying it, or creating works
based on it requires a commercial license. After 60 days, continued use
requires a signed commercial license.

## Commercial licenses

Commercial licenses cover use of the official compiled release
artifacts (binaries, wheels, and linking against the C ABI) and include
source rights only for the wrapper and integration layer — the Python
binding (including the PySpark data source), SQL UDF definitions, and
integration examples — so licensees can read, adapt, and deploy the
integration code they operate. Commercial licenses do not include
rights to compile, modify, or create works based on the core (Zig)
source.

For commercial license inquiries, contact: laurent.fabre@gmail.com

